v0.099: password reset (forgot password / reset via email)

Logins can now have an optional email address:
- Settings > Users lets you add one when creating a new login, or add/edit
  the email on an existing one (email is unique across logins, enforced in
  application code so the error message can stay friendly).
- "Forgot password?" on the sign-in page sends a one-time reset link to
  that address, through the shared Settings > Email account. The link is
  valid for one hour and single-use - resetting the password also retires
  any other still-live link for the same login.
- Deliberately silent about whether a given name/email actually matched
  anything, so this can't be used to enumerate valid logins. The endpoint
  is rate limited (SimpleRateLimiter, 5 attempts / 15 min per client IP) as
  basic abuse protection now that this app is internet-facing - it's the
  first genuinely public, unauthenticated write endpoint this system has
  had.
- New "Public URL" setting under Settings > Email, for deployments behind
  a reverse proxy or tunnel where the backend can't otherwise tell it's
  being reached over HTTPS (request.getScheme() sees "http" through
  Cloudflare Tunnel/nginx here) - keeps reset links from coming out with
  the wrong scheme.

Backend: V45 migration (users.email, password_reset_tokens), User/
UserRepository, PasswordResetToken(+Repository), PasswordResetService
(SHA-256 token hashing, same pattern as ApiKeyService), SimpleRateLimiter,
AuthController's new /forgot-password and /reset-password endpoints,
SecurityConfig permitAll additions, UserController's new PUT .../email
endpoint and CreateUserRequest.email.

Frontend: Login.tsx forgot-password flow, new /reset-password page, and
Settings.tsx Users section email UI (add on create, add/edit on existing).

Also updated docs/BNS_Warehouse_Setup_Guide.pdf (Users, and a new
Section 6.3) and README.

